data.content:
The `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` 10.0 package upgraded its dependency from **OpenAPI.NET v1** to **OpenAPI.NET v2** (`Microsoft.OpenApi` 2.x). This is a major breaking change affecting the object model. Here's what changed and how to fix each piece:

---

## 1. `OpenApiString` / `OpenApiAny` removed

OpenAPI.NET v2 replaced `IOpenApiAny`/`OpenApiString` with `JsonNode`.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After (.NET 10)
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

Remove `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;` — the namespace no longer exists.

---

## 2. `OpenApiResponse` → responses use string description only (no change needed structurally, but check constructors)

This line likely still compiles, but if you get errors, ensure you're using the updated namespace. The `OpenApiResponse` API is largely the same in v2.

---

## 3. `OpenApiReference.Type` is now `ReferenceType` → `string`

In v2, `OpenApiReference` changed. `Type` is removed in favor of setting the `Id` directly, or you use the new constructor:

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
{
    Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
};

// After (.NET 10)
var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme();
oAuthScheme.Ref = "oauth2";  // or use a JSON $ref path
```

Or use the reference as a key directly — the v2 model supports `OpenApiSecurityScheme` with just an `Id` reference.

---

## 4. `schema.Nullable` removed

OpenAPI v3.1 (which v2 of the library targets) replaced `nullable: true` with a type array including `"null"`. The `Nullable` property no longer exists.

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After (.NET 10) — to mark as nullable you'd add "null" to the type:
// To ensure NOT nullable, no action needed (absence of "null" in Type means non-nullable)
// To explicitly remove nullable if present:
property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

`Type` is now a flags enum (`JsonSchemaType`). To **add** nullable: `property.Value.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null;`

---

## 5. `schema.Required` is now `ISet<string>` → `HashSet<string>` (minor)

This likely still works, but the collection type may have changed. `Contains` should still compile.

---

## Summary of required using changes

```csharp
// Remove:
// using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;

// Add:
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
```

## Fixed code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme();
    oAuthScheme.Ref = "oauth2";

    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

The core theme: OpenAPI.NET v2 aligns with **OpenAPI 3.1 / JSON Schema 2020-12**, so `nullable` becomes a type union, primitives become `JsonNode`, and references are simplified.
